##  Understanding `for` Loop Internally

I learned that a `for` loop internally works with an iterator.

```text
Iterable
   ↓
iter()
   ↓
Iterator
   ↓
next()
   ↓
Get value
   ↓
next()
   ↓
Get next value
   ↓
StopIteration
   ↓
Loop automatically stops
```

##  Key Learning

```text
Iterable → Can be looped over
Iterator → Produces values one at a time
iter()   → Creates an iterator
next()   → Gets the next value
StopIteration → No values remaining
```
